# Object-store Parquet integration example

This is a template. Bucket names, prefixes, endpoints, schemas and credentials
belong in private deployment configuration and its approved knowledge snapshot.
Use an object store only when the task and configured access policy authorize it.

The generic sandbox includes DuckDB and its httpfs extension under
`/usr/local/share/duckdb-extensions`. A deployment can provide a host-side gateway
and scoped credentials. Never put real upstream access keys in a public skill.

Restrict scans to requested prefixes/partitions and columns. Do not infer storage
layout or business metrics from examples. Write large results into the workspace
and report the path rather than streaming unbounded rows into the conversation.
